CloudBurrow patch 81 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1624). Needs patches 0018 (_PARTITION_STREAMED),
0016 (_PARTITION_BUFFERED) and 0014's AddTableData (#1340 defaults).

The CloudBurrow front gives each streamed row its stream time
(_PARTITION_STREAMED), which DML reads, and a row of a partitioned table
its place in the streaming buffer (_PARTITIONTIME and _PARTITIONDATE NULL,
or _PARTITION_BUFFERED). tabledata.insertAll could not give a row a
pseudo-column, so the front streamed every insert into a scratch table,
moved the rows with INSERT ... SELECT, and deleted the scratch table; that
DROP rebuilt googlesqlite's whole catalog (resetCatalog), which grows with
every table the engine holds: through the official Go client, a 10-row
insert took 42 ms p50 in an empty project and 115 ms (p99 289 ms) in a
project of 150 datasets of three tables.

tabledata.insertAll now reads the request header
X-Cloudburrow-Stream-Columns, a JSON object of pseudo-column names
(_PARTITION_STREAMED, _PARTITIONTIME, _PARTITIONDATE, _PARTITION_BUFFERED)
to a value for every row, or to a list of one value per row of the
request, and the rows' INSERT gives each its literal; rows that give the
same values go in by one statement, in their order, as rows that give the
same columns do. A header it cannot read is 400 invalid, and nothing is
inserted. Without the header nothing changes. The regression test
(server/cloudburrow_stream_columns_test.go) fails without the patch.

